# C / C++ coding style

Narrows `core-common-rules`' stack-agnostic style rules to modern C++
(17/20/23) and modern C idiom, following the C++ Core Guidelines. Applies to
both `.c`/`.h` and `.cpp`/`.cc`/`.cxx`/`.hpp`/`.hxx` files.

## Naming and structure

- `snake_case` for functions, variables, and namespaces; `PascalCase` for
  types; `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for macros and compile-time constants; an
  established project convention wins over this default.
- A header is self-contained: `#pragma once` (or a project-consistent include
  guard) and every symbol it uses `#include`d, not pulled in transitively.
- A translation unit's private helpers go in an anonymous namespace (C++) or
  are `static` (C).

## Modern C++ idiom (17/20/23)

- `std::unique_ptr` by default; `std::shared_ptr` only for genuinely shared
  ownership.
- `std::make_unique`/`std::make_shared` over a bare `new` passed to a smart
  pointer constructor.
- `std::span` (C++20) for a non-owning view over a contiguous range instead
  of a raw `(pointer, length)` pair.
- Move, don't copy, when ownership transfers: by-value plus `std::move`, or
  an rvalue-reference overload.
- Range-`for` or `<ranges>` (C++20) over a manual index loop for plain
  traversal; keep the manual iterator form where the iterator itself is
  needed.
- `constexpr`/`consteval` for anything computable at compile time; no
  `#define` for a typed constant.

## Modern C safety practices

- `snprintf`, not `sprintf`; `strncpy`/explicit length checks, not
  `strcpy`/`strcat`; `fgets`, never `gets`; every buffer write states or
  checks its destination's capacity.
- Check every `malloc`/`calloc`/`realloc` return for `NULL`; on `realloc`
  failure keep the original pointer.
- C99 designated initializers and fixed arrays with an explicit, checked
  bound over a raw pointer with a length carried in a comment.
- `const`-qualify a pointer parameter the function does not mutate through
  (`const char *`).

## Formatting

- Format with the project's `clang-format`/`.clang-format` if present; do
  not hand-format around it.
- Brace placement follows the project's existing style.
